I fixed both parts of #1045 and committed them as Day 242 (20:47): Fixes #1045 …. Build, the full cargo test run, clippy with -D warnings and the fmt check all pass.

1. The `/doctor` project-context row now shows refused files. The code that builds the row used to throw away the list of instruction files the directory fence refuses. A refused CLAUDE.md simply vanished from the row. If every file was refused, the row said "create YOYO.md or run /init", which is wrong advice because the file exists. The row now comes from a new function, project_context_check, which names each refused file using the same wording as /context: CLAUDE.md (refused by the directory fence: …). Cleaning up control characters in the reason happens in that shared code. When every file is refused, the row is a warning that names those files and gives no create-a-file advice.

2. `yoyo doctor` in the shell now applies the fence. It used to pass an empty fence, so [directories] deny in .yoyo.toml and --deny-dir were ignored. I moved the code that builds the startup fence (--allow-dir/--deny-dir, falling back to [directories]) out of parse_permission_and_dir_config into a new cli::startup_dir_restrictions. Both the session and shell yoyo doctor now call it, so there is one construction and the change stayed small. Two things are still not applied on the shell: --restricted, because doctor doesn't accept that flag, and lists added by /cd, which only exist inside a session.

Tests:
• A new src/commands_dev_tests.rs covers: a refused file next to a loaded one, all files refused on both the REPL and shell surfaces, a reason containing an escape character being cleaned, and the case with nothing refused, which is checked with assert_eq! on the full string to be byte-identical to the old output.
• A real-binary test in tests/integration.rs runs yoyo doctor with a config deny, then with --deny-dir, then with no fence (which must still list the file as loaded). It runs with provider keys removed from the environment, like the other tests there.
• Positive control: with the refused-file rendering disabled, both refusal unit tests and the real-binary test failed by name. The escape-character test stayed green, because it only checks that something is absent, so a dropped row can't make it fail. After restoring the code everything passed, and no NEUTERED marker is left.

Docs: docs/src/configuration/permissions.md said /doctor "leaves it out of its project-context row", which is now false, so I rewrote it to describe both surfaces. I also added a Day-242 note to the commands_dev.rs entry in ARCHITECTURE.md. The only #1045 mentions in src and docs are the code comments I added, so no user-facing pointer will go stale when the issue closes.

The issue gets closed by the Fixes #1045 in the commit title when it's pushed. I don't know of anything left over that needs a comment on it.
